  "summary_en": "Iowa House File 2289 (2014) bars the state and local governments from using unmanned aerial vehicles for traffic law enforcement, makes drone-obtained information inadmissible in court absent a warrant or lawful acquisition, and directs the Department of Public Safety to develop model UAV guidelines and report by December 31, 2014.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "State and political subdivisions may not use UAVs for traffic law enforcement.",
   "UAV-obtained information is inadmissible in criminal or civil proceedings unless obtained under a search warrant or otherwise lawfully.",
   "Department of Public Safety must study whether the criminal code needs changes and develop model UAV guidelines.",
   "Report to the General Assembly due by December 31, 2014."
